2026-10-29T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2339) 'a persona answers from a goal-task network instead of from weights
 # tags: rfd:feature, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-29T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2339) 'the persona repository, the planner it requires as a library, and its register row
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-29T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2339) 'A persona answers from a goal-task network, so a goal gives an exact plan with no sampling.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-29T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2339) 'A request in words reaches a persona only by way of whoever authors the domain. A domain with a thin vocabulary answers a thin set of goals.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-29T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2339) 'Read RFD66606-2292 next, the organization domain this workspace's RFDs render into.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-29T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2339) 'a persona answers from a planning domain
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-29T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2339) '- A persona answers from a goal-task network rather than from weights: a domain and a goal go in, an exact plan comes out, and no sampling is involved (operator, 2026-10-30).
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-29T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2339) '- The persona is the instinct model: Lean 4 code, named for its latency against a language model (operator, 2026-10-29).
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-29T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2339) '- The planner is a library, not a reference. The persona requires the RECTGTN domain over GitHub, as the character domain does, and composes in its shared GTN space.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-29T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2339) '- Its inputs are a code or a number. A code is the vocabulary: one level count a dimension, packed mixed-radix, the shape residual FSQ stacks its stages in.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-29T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2339) '- A code the codebook does not hold, a variable the domain does not declare, and a goal the domain cannot reach are refused by name.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-29T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2339) '- RFD66606-2292, the organization domain this workspace's own RFDs render into.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-29T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2339) '- RFD66606-2232, the renderer that turns an RFD into a planning problem.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-29T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2339) 'Where it lives
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-29T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2339) 'It is its own repository on the interactor side, placed when it is created, and the planner revision it builds against is recorded in its manifest.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-29T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2339) 'What landed
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-29T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2339) 'The persona is a Lean package of its own: a domain of state variables, a codebook and actions, a goal over the planner's own node space, and a search that composes the plan. The landing subject is "Compose the persona in Lean over the planner library".
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-29T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2339) 'Its gate is a witness exe with a positive and a negative control per invariant: the codebook's size, basis and mixed-radix index; a code past its level and a code of the wrong arity both refused; a plan that executes to the goal; and three refusals, an unreachable goal, an undeclared variable and zero fuel.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-29T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2339) 'The codebook is the vocabulary
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-29T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2339) 'Eight levels over four dimensions is 4096 codes a stage, and four stages of those is 281474976710656 codes from thirty-two small integers. A code is what a goal argument binds, and a number is the other half of the surface.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-29T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2339) 'The codec is the one this workspace already certifies for the residual-FSQ recommender: a mixed-radix index over per-dimension levels, injective and bounded at the real scale.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-29T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2339) 'References
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-29T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2339) 'The codebook's shape and the stages it stacks come from this lineage.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-29T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2339) '- Zeghidour et al., SoundStream (doi 10.1109/TASLP.2021.3130651)
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-29T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2339) '- Défossez et al., EnCodec (doi 10.48550/arXiv.2210.13438)
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-29T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2339) '- Mentzer et al., Finite Scalar Quantization (doi 10.48550/arXiv.2309.15505)
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-29T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2339) '- Zhu et al., Robust Residual FSQ (doi 10.48550/arXiv.2508.15860)
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-29T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2339) '- Liu et al., VQTalker (doi 10.48550/arXiv.2412.09892)
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-29T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2339) 'The design's other half
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-29T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2339) 'The persona is the half that answers from a program. The other half is a language model, and the design keeps a place for it until the model has a home (operator, 2026-10-29).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-29T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2339) 'Code as data, and what a persona says back
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-29T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2339) 'A caller gives category and numeric instructions, and the persona walks the programs it holds: "you did not even weight paint", then what face tracking costs. The caller is given options, and a choice fits the input shape rather than arriving in words. A failure and a success each point at a guide, baked in or linked (operator, 2026-10-29).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-29T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2339) 'What is not known
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-29T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-2339) '- How a persona composes with this workspace's rendered problems, which the organization domain answers today through the planner's Elixir consumer.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-29T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-2339) '- The temporal reading of a domain that declares no reads and no writes: the plan order is exact, and the timeline parallelizes what the domain leaves undeclared.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-29T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-2339) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-29T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-2339) 'A persona cannot answer a question that is not a goal.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2339  1 LINE
 Text:Written

